WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.519
As we all try to make sense of Season 2's
huge cliffhanger, there's one character who

00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:09.940
may be much more important to the future of
the Umbrella Academy than any of us realised.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.190
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining why Harlan could

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:19.410
well be a secret member of the Sparrow Academy,
and revealing hidden clues to his potential

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:20.980
backstory with the Commission.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.259
Obviously, spoilers ahead so take care.

00:00:23.259 --> 00:00:28.130
In Harlan's very last scene of Season 2, we
see him leaving Dallas with his mother Sissy.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.949
And although Vanya had seemingly withdrawn
the powers she transferred to him when he

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:36.829
drowned, the final moment left us in no doubt
that Harlan has retained some of her telekinetic

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:37.829
powers.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:42.140
And we saw him levitating his little wooden
bird, a strong pointer to a connection between

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.640
him and the Sparrow Academy.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.710
But what would be Harlan's role in the Sparrow
team?

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:53.070
Although he's just a young boy in 1963, 56
years later in 2019 Harlan would be well over

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.350
sixty years old.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:59.300
So, rather than Harlan getting recruited by
Hargreeves in 1989 when the other super-babies

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.660
are born,
it's more likely that Hargreeves finds out

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.070
about Harlan if the young boy's superpowers
show up again later in the 60s.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:10.110
They could begin to work together to set up
a new superhero team, with Harlan becoming

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:13.910
a superhero who dubs himself The Sparrow after
his favourite toy.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:17.980
And that could lead Hargreeves to name the
Sparrow Academy in Harlan's honour, especially

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:22.430
if he dies on a mission, similar to young
Ben in the original timeline.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:26.630
An alternative is that in this new timeline,
the origin of the super-babies is changed

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:30.540
and rather than being born spontaneously as
in the original timeline,

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.150
Harlan is the Sparrows' father and they inherited
their powers from him.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.670
The glowing lights that Hargreeves released
in the finale of Season 1 appear to be behind

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:42.920
both Vanya and Harlan's powers, given that
we saw her transfer them into Harlan.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.750
So, just as Vanya was able to reproduce her
powers in another person, what's to say that

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.260
Harlan can't do the same and pass on his powers
to others too?

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:55.370
If Harlan were to die, as I mentioned just
before, he could still live on inside the

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:59.290
mysterious green cube that floats alongside
the Sparrows on the balcony in the finale.

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:03.560
Now, I know this may sound crazy, but it's
not outside the bounds of possibility in the

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.730
bonkers world of the Umbrella Academy
where we've already had a talking, smoking

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:10.950
goldfish living in a fishbowl attached to
a robotic body.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:15.160
We know Harlan has telekinetic powers and
can therefore make objects float, so it's

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:19.610
interesting that the cube not only floats
into view, but it also glows inside hinting

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.170
that it may be sentient.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:26.120
And, curiously, the first time we see Harlan
in the show, he's actually wearing green.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.670
Indeed, there's a precedent for something
similar to this in another superhero show,

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:31.670
Doom Patrol.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.319
In that DC show, the body of Cliff Steele
was destroyed beyond repair in a car accident,

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:41.600
however, his brain was salvaged, kept alive
and put into a robot body, turning him into

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.600
Robotman.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:47.650
And the Doom Patrol comics were a major influence
on Gerard Way when he wrote the original Umbrella

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:48.650
Academy comics.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:52.510
So, even if Harlan were fatally wounded on
a mission, Hargreeves could have saved his

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.260
consciousness and transferred it into the
cube.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:59.069
We've already seen Hargreeves save Luther
from death by injecting him with a serum that

00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:02.069
changes his physiology into something more
ape-like.

00:03:02.069 --> 00:03:06.840
And in Season 2, Hargreeves also brought Pogo
back from the dead in a similar way.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.400
Alternatively, Harlan could still be alive
and using his powers to control the cube himself.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.900
Another possibility hinted at within the show
is that Harlan becomes involved with the Commission.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.840
When his powers blew up in the penultimate
episode of Season 2, it showed up as a major

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.850
timeline anomaly on the Commission's Infinite
Switchboard.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:28.270
The Handler immediately recognised the significance
of this event, and she told Harlan that she

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.069
could take him somewhere that would understand
and help him.

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:35.800
"I can take you to a place where you will
be properly understood, listened to, even

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.800
without a voice.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:43.340
I can tap into your potential, and together,
just the two of us, we can do incredible things."

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.490
Now, Harlan may have only spoken a few times
in Season 2, but it was shown that he could

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.180
understand the conversations around him and
whatever was being said to him.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:55.560
So, the Handler's words to him may well have
planted an idea or a question in his mind

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.500
about who she was, where she came from and
what the place was that she was referring

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.500
to.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.760
We also know in the finale from Herb that
the Commission will be looking for a new board

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:06.730
of directors and therefore a new head of the
organisation.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:11.770
So, when Harlan's powers likely show up again
on the Infinite Switchboard, I expect the

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.460
Commission to take an interest in him again.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:17.540
He may even get recruited to work for them,
similar to how the Handler recruited Five

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.930
as a Commission agent in the first season.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:24.870
In fact, Harlan's name may actually be a reference
to Andrew Harlan, the protagonist from Isaac

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:29.669
Asimov's The End of Eternity, a novel which
has some incredible parallels with The Umbrella

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:30.669
Academy.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:34.779
The End of Eternity is a time-travel story
in which people called the Eternals run an

00:04:34.779 --> 00:04:38.999
organisation that exists outside of time
and manipulates events throughout history

00:04:38.999 --> 00:04:43.449
to create and maintain what they see as an
optimum timeline that will bring about the

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.360
maximum good for humanity.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.610
Ring any bells so far?

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.010
"So the Commission controls time?"

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:51.180
"More like we maintain the correct timeline,
but basically yeah."

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:57.050
"We are tasked with the preservation of the
time continuum through manipulation and removals."

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:01.069
In Asimov's novel, Harlan is an Eternal and
Technician who makes modifications to the

00:05:01.069 --> 00:05:02.069
human timeline.

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:07.110
And I can't help but think that the connection
between The Umbrella Academy's Temps Commission,

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:11.650
or as it's called in the comics,
and Asimov's Eternals hints at Harlan ending

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.189
up at the Commission in some way, maybe even
taking charge.

00:05:15.189 --> 00:05:19.520
And if he does, perhaps he will become instrumental
in ensuring the Commission follows a policy

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.159
that leads to the creation of the Sparrow
Academy.

00:05:22.159 --> 00:05:27.569
Another small but important detail from the
finale of season 2 is that as Sissy and Harlan

00:05:27.569 --> 00:05:32.360
leave Texas for California, we see them crossing
the state border into New Mexico.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:36.569
New Mexico is, of course, en route from Texas
to California, but it's interesting that the

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:40.110
series choses to show us this particular moment
in the journey,

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:44.099
because it means that Sissy and Harlan could
be passing near to the site of the Roswell

00:05:44.099 --> 00:05:49.419
UFO incident which has been the subject of
numerous UFO and alien conspiracy theories.

00:05:49.419 --> 00:05:54.280
The Umbrella Academy already made allusions
to various JFK assassination conspiracy theories

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:57.849
in Season 2,
and given the reveal of Hargreeves as an alien,

00:05:57.849 --> 00:06:02.669
the show may be hinting at something strange
happening to Harlan as he passes through New

00:06:02.669 --> 00:06:03.669
Mexico.

00:06:03.669 --> 00:06:06.940
Could he be intercepted by the Commission,
or somebody connected to the now deceased

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:10.659
Majestic 12 or some other nefarious organisation?

00:06:10.659 --> 00:06:14.960
We've got numerous possibilities pointing
towards Harlan either setting up or helping

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.680
form the Sparrow Academy, perhaps even being
the cube member of the team,

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:22.490
but is there anything that suggests that he'll
be a future antagonist in the series?

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:26.889
Well, it's interesting to note that at the
end of Season 2, when new Ben arrives on the

00:06:26.889 --> 00:06:30.039
scene, he's immediately rude and hostile towards
the Umbrella team.

00:06:30.039 --> 00:06:32.740
"Dad, who the hell are these assholes?"

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:37.690
We know that Reginald Hargreeves is a cold
and unforgiving father as we've seen in flashbacks

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:39.249
from both seasons.

00:06:39.249 --> 00:06:42.870
And he even admitted to Luther that he has
a deep dislike of children.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:47.129
And given how he reacted to the Umbrella team
that he met in 1963.

00:06:47.129 --> 00:06:48.259
"I've seen about enough."

00:06:48.259 --> 00:06:53.379
It's clear that he must have decided to form
the Sparrow Academy with very different children.

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:57.960
Given the way new Ben has turned out in comparison
to the much more gentle Ben from the first

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:02.240
two seasons, it seems like this new group
may have grown up with a nastier and colder

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:03.240
edge to them.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:08.229
Which is why the Sparrows and possibly Harlan
may turn out to be Season 3's antagonists.

00:07:08.229 --> 00:07:13.029
On the outside, they may seem to be superheroes,
but behind the scenes they may have a darker

00:07:13.029 --> 00:07:17.039
side, similar perhaps to the corrupt nature
of the superheroes in The Boys.

00:07:17.039 --> 00:07:21.439
We should also remember that Harlan inherited
Vanya's powers and she became an antagonist

00:07:21.439 --> 00:07:24.849
in the first season due to the way she'd been
treated by her father and family.

00:07:24.849 --> 00:07:30.699
In situations of extreme emotional distress,
Vanya's powers can spiral out of control,

00:07:30.699 --> 00:07:34.949
something we also saw when she was being tortured
by the FBI in Season 2.

00:07:34.949 --> 00:07:39.229
Harlan also went supernova when he accidentally
caused the death of his father after his powers

00:07:39.229 --> 00:07:40.979
deflected a bullet into Carl.

00:07:40.979 --> 00:07:45.199
However, after Vanya extracted the lights
from Harlan, he seems to be calmer and more

00:07:45.199 --> 00:07:49.669
in control, but we don't know whether he can
keep the powers in check if some kind of tragedy

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:50.879
strikes again.

00:07:50.879 --> 00:07:54.789
What if the authorities come after Sissy and
him when they investigate Carl's death and

00:07:54.789 --> 00:07:56.849
try to take her away from him, for instance?

00:07:56.849 --> 00:08:01.250
Of course, I don't think it's at all certain
that Harlan will end up on the dark side,

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:05.999
especially because in all of his Season 2
scenes with Vanya, he seemed sweet and sensitive.

00:08:05.999 --> 00:08:10.979
Still, there is something a little ominous
about the final scene as we see him and Sissy

00:08:10.979 --> 00:08:13.439
cross the border into New Mexico.

